13. Host memory visibility in the execution desktop. The five protected data
    trees agents, user-memory, workflows, plugins and managed-skills are
    mounted only below the protected /data/runtime/host-data root;
    agent-transcripts and other Host-only data stay out of Box.
    host/release/data_init.py changes ownership and mode only on directories
    it creates. host/release/backup.py validates exact mounts.
    host/runtime/prompt-runtime.mjs preserves proactive memory retrieval, adds
    its live-access reminder only when the mounts are present and falls back
    to the original prompt when the extra text exceeds the size limit.
    Distribution version suffixes are accepted and --host-only is not gated.
    Contributed by @jun9100 (GitHub pull request #5). Clients are unchanged.
    Since 1.15.0 the mounts are read-only and live in a separate
    host/release/compose.memory.yaml, which deploy.py adds only with Docker
    Engine 26.0+, API 1.45+ and Compose 2.26.0+ and otherwise skips; from
    upstream, see below. 1.7.0 to 1.14.0 mounted them writable in
    compose.yaml. ProkBot Plus lets the checks before an update and backups
    accept those writable mounts so that update can replace them.
    Since 1.15.1 host/runtime/host-attachments.mjs no longer copies managed
    attachments into a Box that already reads them through the read-only
    mount; the copy failed with a read-only file system error in 1.15.0.

