20. Host turn continuity and working-indicator reliability.
    - host/runtime/turn-continuity.mjs (new), recovered-host-flow.mjs,
      recovered-engine.mjs, recovered-harness.mjs, recovered-host-execution.mjs
      and model-errors.mjs: detect substantive unreported tool work after
      multi-SendToUser, tool-first, parallel or plain-text/reasoning endings
      (excluding bookkeeping tools such as update_state and TodoWrite) with
      bounded closing continuations (up to 2); enable in-loop
      empty/missing-SendToUser retries for normal user turns only (excluding
      subagents, isSilenceAllowed runs and group-member turns) capped at 2 per
      turn; map output length truncation to OutputTokensLimitExceededError for
      one automatic continuation per step while preserving the truncation
      error; and keep live session activity populated at turn start and across
      mid-turn SendToUser updates so clients consistently display working state.
    - Contributed by @jun9100 (GitHub pull request #18).

21. Model context and reasoning-effort sync with overflow self-healing.
    - host/runtime/model-specs.mjs (new), model-context-cache.mjs (new),
      model-policy.mjs, model-routing.mjs, model-session.mjs, model-errors.mjs,
      config.mjs and host-extensions.mjs: per-profile contextMode and
      effortsMode ("auto" | "manual", manual when omitted, including legacy
      model.env); auto profiles follow the context window (at least 1024) and
      reasoning efforts reported by the provider's /models and the ceiling
      observed in comparison-style or repeated overflow errors, kept for 30
      days; route efforts outside the reported list step down to the nearest
      supported level, never to none; the admin service and the Host runtime
      write separate files (model-context-cache.json and
      model-context-observed.json); input-limit errors are recognised in more
      provider formats, and rate-limit errors are no longer taken for them.
    - host/server/models.mjs, index.mjs, public/model.js, public/locales-en.js
      and host/tools/host-admin.mjs: startup, save-triggered and 6-hour
      background /models sync only for providers with an auto profile, behind
      an admin switch (on by default); an optional Codex client-version probe
      (off by default); POST /admin/api/model/resolve (rate-limited),
      sync-contexts, PUT sync-settings and POST observed/clear; built-in
      reference values shown only as suggestions; host-admin model-set saves
      manual only when --context or --efforts is given.
    - Contributed by @jun9100 (GitHub pull request #19).

